-- long plain text paragraphs inside comments
-- The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog while the compiler scans every word boundary.
-- Readability matters because generated documentation ships to users in many contexts and themes.
-- Plain identifiers must stay unwrapped so ordinary code does not drown in low-value spans.
-- Compound operators should remain one visual token instead of a chain of separate characters.
-- Contextual roles only appear when bounded lexical evidence supports them without semantic claims.
-- ALL_CAPS constants such as PI TAU and E stay plain unless a real contract list surrounds them.
-- Unicode identifiers and strings must survive escaping without splitting surrogate pairs.

